// A NON-PUB METHOD IS REFUSED ON THE LIBRARY'S OWN RECORD (`@FR-F-Surface`).  `fn fs_rm(self: FsP)`
// is declared without `pub`; a program holding a pub `FsP` reaches only the surface, so
// `p.fs_rm()` must be refused — the method spelling is a reach of the item like the qualifier.
//
// Guards loft#2115: accepted there and printed 7 on both backends (FsP{4}.x + 3) — the method
// spelling finds every method of the receiver type, and nothing asked its `pub`.
//
// @falsified-at: e71f24b34 — accepted there (prints 7), interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the item and the library.
// HOLDS: `a-non-pub-function-is-refused-through-the-qualifier` beside it.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: fs_rm

use f_surface_fixture_lib::*;

fn main() {
  p = FsP { x: 4 };
  println("{p.fs_rm()}");
}
